„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections—…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§Moreover thou shalt make the tabernacle with ten curtains of fine twined linen, and blue, and purple, and scarlet: with cherubims of cunning work shalt thou make them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThe length of one curtain shall be eight and twenty cubits, and the breadth of one curtain four cubits: and every one of the curtains shall have one measure.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtThe five curtains shall be coupled together one to another; and other five curtains shall be coupled one to another.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙËAnd thou shalt make loops of blue upon the edge of the one curtain from the selvedge in the coupling; and likewise shalt thou make in the uttermost edge of another curtain, in the coupling of the second.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾Fifty loops shalt thou make in the one curtain, and fifty loops shalt thou make in the edge of the curtain that is in the coupling of the second; that the loops may take hold one of another.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{And thou shalt make fifty taches of gold, and couple the curtains together with the taches: and it shall be one tabernacle.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrAnd thou shalt make curtains of goats' hair to be a covering upon the tabernacle: eleven curtains shalt thou make.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’The length of one curtain shall be thirty cubits, and the breadth of one curtain four cubits: and the eleven curtains shall be all of one measure.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™And thou shalt couple five curtains by themselves, and six curtains by themselves, and shalt double the sixth curtain in the forefront of the tabernacle.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
