„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd thou shalt make fifty taches of brass, and put the taches into the loops, and couple the tent together, that it may be one.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒAnd the remnant that remaineth of the curtains of the tent, the half curtain that remaineth, shall hang over the backside of the tabernacle.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙØAnd a cubit on the one side, and a cubit on the other side of that which remaineth in the length of the curtains of the tent, it shall hang over the sides of the tabernacle on this side and on that side, to cover it.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlAnd thou shalt make a covering for the tent of rams' skins dyed red, and a covering above of badgers' skins.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses›„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJAnd thou shalt make boards for the tabernacle of shittim wood standing up.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdTen cubits shall be the length of a board, and a cubit and a half shall be the breadth of one board.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„Two tenons shall there be in one board, set in order one against another: thus shalt thou make for all the boards of the tabernacle.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]And thou shalt make the boards for the tabernacle, twenty boards on the south side southward.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬And thou shalt make forty sockets of silver under the twenty boards; two sockets under one board for his two tenons, and two sockets under another board for his two tenons.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYAnd for the second side of the tabernacle on the north side there shall be twenty boards:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdand their forty sockets of silver; two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHAnd for the sides of the tabernacle westward thou shalt make six boards.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRAnd two boards shalt thou make for the corners of the tabernacle in the two sides.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙµAnd they shall be coupled together beneath, and they shall be coupled together above the head of it unto one ring: thus shall it be for them both; they shall be for the two corners.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd they shall be eight boards, and their sockets of silver, sixteen sockets; two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`And thou shalt make bars of shittim wood; five for the boards of the one side of the tabernacle,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™and five bars for the boards of the other side of the tabernacle, and five bars for the boards of the side of the tabernacle, for the two sides westward.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJAnd the middle bar in the midst of the boards shall reach from end to end.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd thou shalt overlay the boards with gold, and make their rings of gold for places for the bars: and thou shalt overlay the bars with gold.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd thou shalt rear up the tabernacle according to the fashion thereof which was shewed thee in the mount.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse#¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„And thou shalt make a vail of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen of cunning work: with cherubims shall it be made:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹and thou shalt hang it upon four pillars of shittim wood overlaid with gold: their hooks shall be of gold, upon the four sockets of silver.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÊAnd thou shalt hang up the vail under the taches, that thou mayest bring in thither within the vail the ark of the testimony: and the vail shall divide unto you between the holy place and the most holy.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWAnd thou shalt put the mercy seat upon the ark of the testimony in the most holy place.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹And thou shalt set the table without the vail, and the candlestick over against the table on the side of the tabernacle toward the south: and thou shalt put the table on the north side.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book§chapter«first_verse$ªlast_verse%¦verses’„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠAnd thou shalt make an hanging for the door of the tent, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, wrought with needlework.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ³And thou shalt make for the hanging five pillars of shittim wood, and overlay them with gold, and their hooks shall be of gold: and thou shalt cast five sockets of brass for them.¦layout ªlast_verse%